class DataProcessor implements Runnable {
    private final String name;
    DataProcessor(String name) { this.name = name; }

    @Override
    public void run() {
        System.out.println(name + " on: " + Thread.currentThread().getName());
    }
}

var t1 = new Thread(new DataProcessor("Task1"));
var t2 = new Thread(new DataProcessor("Task2"));

t1.run();   // BAD: runs on main, blocks until done
t2.run();   // BAD: runs on main after Task1 finishes
// Both print "... on: main" -- sequential, no concurrency
```

```java
var t1 = new Thread(new DataProcessor("Task1"));
var t2 = new Thread(new DataProcessor("Task2"));

t1.start();  // GOOD: new thread, runs concurrently
t2.start();  // GOOD: another thread, both run in parallel
// Prints "... on: Thread-0" and "... on: Thread-1" -- interleaved
```
*The thread name printed inside `run()` is the simplest way to prove which path you took.*

