class OrderService implements AutoCloseable {
    private final ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10);

    void processOrders(List<Order> orders) {
        for (Order order : orders) {
            executor.submit(() -> processOrder(order));
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void close() {
        executor.shutdown();
        try {
            if (!executor.awaitTermination(60, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {
                executor.shutdownNow(); // requests interruption; does not force termination
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            executor.shutdownNow();
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        }
    }
}
```

`newFixedThreadPool(10)` bounds active worker count but normally uses an unbounded work queue. If queued load must also be bounded, configure a `ThreadPoolExecutor` or another execution policy with explicit capacity and rejection behavior.

